    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Solve the following. $$\\frac{x+1}{x^2-x}-\\frac2{x-1}=\\frac3x.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No solution.\n\nClearing the denominators gives $x=1$, which makes an original denominator zero.",
      "worked": "The original denominators require $x\\ne0,1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x+1-2x}{x(x-1)}&=\\frac{3(x-1)}{x(x-1)}\\\\x+1-2x&=3(x-1)\\\\1-x&=3x-3\\\\4&=4x\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $x=1$ is excluded, there is no solution.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
